<title>FRANCE: Bus carrying British children crashes in France.</title>
<headline>Bus carrying British children crashes in France.</headline>
<dateline>GRENOBLE, France 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Two people were killed and three others seriously injured when a bus carrying British children veered off a road in eastern France on Monday, police said.</p>
<p>The bus left the road near the town of Notre-Dame du Pre and fell 20 metres (60 feet). Another 17 people were less seriously injured.</p>
<p>The identity of the victims and the cause of the accident were not immediately known.</p>
